  "title": "Thiago Pitarch suffers knee injury, out around two months",
  "publication_date": "2026-07-27T05:52:51+00:00",
  "summary": "Real Madrid midfielder Thiago Pitarch suffered a left-knee ligament injury in his first training session after rejoining the squad and will be sidelined for about two months. The setback forces the club to accelerate a decision on whether to loan or transfer him for the 2026-27 season and may reduce interest from other clubs.",
  "content": "Real Madrid midfielder Thiago Pitarch suffered a knee injury during his very first training session after rejoining the squad and will be out around two months. The injury affected ligaments on his left knee.\n\nThe injury complicates Real Madrid's decision about his future. The coaching staff had planned to evaluate his performances in the coming weeks to decide whether the midfielder would benefit from spending the 2026-2027 season at another club. With Pitarch injured, the club will have to make that decision sooner, and the injury may reduce interest from potential suitors.\n\nEither way, it appears Pitarch could still be playing elsewhere this upcoming season, given he needs significant playing time to develop and improve his game.\n\nPitarch had just rejoined the squad and this setback comes at a pivotal moment in his career, potentially altering short-term development plans and transfer market dynamics.",
